      children: _jsx(_components.code, {
        className: "language-text",
        children: "1. Do not share mutable state unless you have a synchronization strategy.\n2. Prefer immutable objects across thread boundaries.\n3. Use ExecutorService, not random new Thread().\n4. Every pool needs bounded capacity or explicit overload behavior.\n5. Every blocking operation needs timeout/cancellation strategy.\n6. volatile is for visibility, not compound atomicity.\n7. Atomic is for simple independent state, not multi-field invariant.\n8. Locks protect invariants, not just variables.\n9. parallelStream is not for blocking I/O.\n10. Virtual threads are excellent for blocking I/O, but still need bulkheads.\n11. ThreadLocal must be cleaned with remove().\n12. Context propagation must be designed, not assumed.\n13. Transaction/security/request context should not accidentally cross threads.\n14. Async failures must be observable.\n15. Thread dumps and JFR are mandatory debugging tools.\n"
      })
    }), "\n", _jsx(_components.hr, {}), "\n", _jsx(_components.h1, {
