    }), "\n", _jsx(_components.pre, {
      children: _jsx(_components.code, {
        className: "language-text",
        children: "Concurrency\n- Overlapping tasks.\n- Useful for I/O, request handling, workflow, messaging.\n\nParallelism\n- Actually simultaneous execution.\n- Useful for CPU-heavy computation.\n\nPlatform Thread\n- Traditional Java thread.\n- More expensive.\n- Use bounded pools.\n\nVirtual Thread\n- Lightweight Java thread, final since JDK 21.\n- Great for blocking I/O.\n- Not a replacement for DB/API limits.\n\nExecutor\n- Manages task execution.\n- Prefer bounded queue and explicit rejection.\n\nCompletableFuture\n- Async composition.\n- Beware executor choice and context propagation.\n\nJava Memory Model\n- Think visibility, atomicity, ordering.\n- happens-before matters.\n\nsynchronized / Lock\n- Protect critical sections and invariants.\n\nvolatile\n- Visibility flag/reference.\n- Not enough for count++.\n\nAtomic\n- Simple lock-free state.\n- Use LongAdder for high-contention counter.\n\nConcurrent Collections\n- Use ConcurrentHashMap, BlockingQueue, CopyOnWriteArrayList where appropriate.\n\nContext\n- Request id, user, tenant, transaction, security, MDC.\n- Does not automatically move across threads.\n- ThreadLocal must be cleared.\n- ScopedValue is the modern scoped immutable context model.\n\nProduction Mindset\n- Bound everything.\n- Timeout everything.\n- Propagate context deliberately.\n- Observe async failures.\n- Debug with thread dump and JFR.\n"
      })
